# meta-deploy.list: the queue meta-deploy.bash runs, in this order.
#
# STANDING RULE (CLAUDE/AgentNotes.md): this list is exactly what needs running NOW. Add a
# run when it is pending, remove it once it has run and is done, leave out what cannot
# usefully run yet, then ask the owner to run meta-deploy.bash. Every step a run needs lives
# in the plan's own scripts, so this is the only command the owner is handed. The order is by
# dependency. A plan with none of triage.bash, deploy.bash and acceptance.bash has nothing
# for the script to do. A triage-only plan is run once, read-only. Words after the folder
# name are passed to that plan's triage.bash, both runs.
#
# One entry per line, three kinds:
#   <plan folder>                  its triage, deploy and acceptance scripts, in order
#   playbooks/<path>.yml           a change no plan owns; run as one unit through its own
#                                  shebang, which goes through run.bash, exactly as
#                                  ./playbooks/imports/<play>.yml does by hand
#   <plan folder>/<script>.bash    one plan script, for a step none of the three fixed names
#                                  fits; run as one unit, like a playbook entry
#
# A line starting with # is a comment and is the description of the entry below it: it is how
# the owner learns what a run will do, so write it. Blank lines are ignored. Any other line
# that is not an entry is a fatal error naming its line number.

# Agent teams: joins the LXC members declared in agent_bus_lxc_members. A team with two LXC
# members whose checkouts are two different repositories, both leaving host and seat to be
# derived, failed here ("gives seat 1 of team <team> to two containers"): seat 1 of one repo and
# seat 1 of another are two handles, and the check between entries now says so. Runs on the
# host_vars as they are; members already joined keep their handles.
# Plan 00201 Task 2.15: helpers/agent_bus/ (declare.py's `settings` and `set`, the team file's
# `removed_humans`) is part of the admin zipapp, so every team reads "out of date (software)"
# until this runs. It installs the new zipapp and stamps each team again. No unit, firewall or
# rendered config changes, so no homeserver is restarted.
playbooks/imports/play-agent-bus.yml
# md-viewer: rebuild and install at main tip 22a55582735d (text on its baseline, dark mode
# and font size settings); asserts `md-viewer --version` carries the new commit.
playbooks/imports/optional/common/play-md-viewer.yml
# ccy 3.99.12.10, container 2.77.7 (each project's image is rebuilt once, at its next ccy
# launch): deploys cc, cc-teams.bash and the ccy launcher, and rebuilds ccy-teams.
# The agent-bus status line shows its teams as 👥 A,B on rows of their own, wrapped at the
# terminal's width, instead of `bus: A,B` appended to the last row, where Claude Code cut it.
# ccy-teams lxc-add: the Checkout step offers the checkouts found in the user's home and walks
# the container's directories with Tab completion, every question names team, step, container
# and user, and the end says how the member starts (agent-bus-claude), whether a running
# session must be restarted, and how to check it live. A container on any LXC store is read.
# Every picker action is a visible, named choice and a key only its shortcut
# (project_hidden_bindings): ccy-sessions gives each session a menu and names its keys in the
# header, the launcher's detached-session offer has a "Start a new session here" row where
# Ctrl-N was the only way, and lxc-add's Tab completion is a listed row with Tab beside it.
# Making a coordinator is one of two questions: a team with none is offered one plainly; a team
# that has one gets a takeover naming the current coordinator, on No (lxc-add too). The picker's
# describe offer is now, not now or never (an old no is asked again once). Launch questions are
# headed by their team ("Team 2 of 3: <team> · ...").
# Plan 00203 M6: cc --teams and the new cc --bus sessions are hot-controlled like ccy ones, also
# from the picker (cc --bus refuses team messages until it is restarted on its first team); a
# membership counts only while its session record carries the bus; pingbus reads no
# PINGBUS_SEATS. Two ccy launches started together in one
# project no longer choose the same container name: each launch claims its name (ccy-teams
# internal claim-container-name, under $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/ccy/container-names/) before podman
# creates it. The image's pingbus status line, cancelled just as it starts the session's own
# status line command, now still kills that command's whole group. Running sessions are not
# touched.
# Plan 00135: it also rebuilds ccy-sessions, so ccy-sessions-set-going.service no longer fails a
# boot for a restored session left to a person (waiting at its SSH passphrase prompt, attached,
# or with text typed); it still fails, naming each, for a real fault such as a launcher that exited.
# Plan 00201 Task 2.15 (ccy 3.99.12.5, container 2.77.4): Enter on a team, then Edit settings,
# opens one screen of the team's fields to change, save and apply (ACCEPTANCE-owner.md step 13).
playbooks/imports/play-claude-yolo.yml
# Plan 00203 acceptance again, every milestone in turn, on ccy 3.99.12.8. M2 starts its two
# throwaway headless sessions (plain and --no-bus) back to back; on 3.99.10.1 both chose the
# same container name and the second failed at podman's create (exit 125). Then M1, M3, M4,
# the new M6 (three throwaway cc sessions on two throwaway teams) and R1-R9, on throwaway teams
# acc-m3a, acc-m3b, acc-m4a, acc-m4b and acc-robust and their sessions, all removed after.
# Prompts for sudo once. Needs ccy launched interactively here once (Quick Launch).
00203-teams-hot-control-and-robustness
# Plan 00203: read-only triage of why team homeservers stop. Changes nothing; reads as root
# (sudo -n): the whole journal, each team's tuwunel.toml (secret values substituted), its
# database size, filesystem and free space, the coredumps, and each running ccy container's
# watcher log. Lists every stop of every agent-bus-hs@ unit with its cause (exit, signal,
# watchdog, OOM, core dump) and who asked (a play, a deploy, an acceptance run, a reboot, the
# health check), then counts deliberate against not deliberate stops per team.
00203-teams-hot-control-and-robustness/triage-hs.bash
# Plan 00170: clears the play ledger's BROKEN marker (runs check_freshness --clear-broken).
# A private play run on 10-12 from a linked worktree was outside that worktree's root, and
# the ledger marked itself BROKEN over it. The ledger now skips such a play with one
# LEDGER-PLAY-NOT-TRACKED line on stderr, so the cause is fixed. Safe: that worktree is gone,
# and only a marker whose reason is that outside-root refusal is cleared; a marker with any
# other reason stays and this entry FAILS, naming it. No marker: nothing to do.
00170-unifi-network-tooling/clear-ledger-broken.bash
